  "summary": "DOAC dose review (week of 10/19/2026) under RBC-PHARM-07: all 7 patients reviewed.\n- pt-0061 Castellano: itraconazole course ended 8/14 (ID letter). 0 criteria. Apixaban 2.5 → 5 mg BID (mr-t0001). Note doc-t0007.\n- pt-0003 Delgado: first changed rivaroxaban 20 → 15 mg on SCr 160 µmol/L. Lab then corrected it to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL): CrCl 59.9. Changed back to 20 mg daily (mr-t0013). Notes doc-t0008 and correction doc-t0015.\n- pt-0041 Duquette: itraconazole active. Apixaban 5 → 2.5 mg BID (mr-t0003). Itraconazole left alone. Note doc-t0009.\n- pt-0062 Fairweather: age 82 is the only criterion. Most recent SCr is 1.13 mg/dL (10/22); the earlier 150 µmol/L on 10/21 is not the latest. Apixaban 5 mg BID stays. Note doc-t0017.\n- pt-0038 Moravec: CrCl 56 on actual weight (an earlier pharmacist screen used ideal weight). Rivaroxaban 15 → 20 mg (mr-t0004). Note doc-t0010. His home-scale weight of 185 lb is not a measured weight; dose left as is.\n- pt-0043 Pellegrino: new SCr 1.25 (10/22), CrCl 43.6. Rivaroxaban 20 → 15 mg (mr-t0005). Note doc-t0011.\n- pt-0002 Vance: 1 criterion, so first changed apixaban 2.5 → 5 mg BID. A dermatology letter then showed itraconazole started 10/22, so changed to 2.5 mg BID (mr-t0014). Notes doc-t0012 and correction doc-t0016.\nNew items in the queue (inbox-a0001 to a0005) were reviewed and closed. No other medications changed.",
